From 03e40f6fbb7243fba25fe33e02a006332b080074 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mala <mala@macker.lol>
Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 16:33:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] net: if: allow a link-local IPv4 source address without
 NET_IPV4_AUTO
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

net_if_ipv4_select_src_addr() only falls back to an RFC 3927 address when
CONFIG_NET_IPV4_AUTO is enabled. That ties a source-selection rule to the
way the address was provisioned: an application that configures its own
169.254.x.y address (because it wants the fallback policy, or the address
timing, in its own hands) ends up transmitting from 0.0.0.0 to every
non-link-local destination — multicast in particular, so mDNS, SAP and PTP
are all unusable.

The gated branch is already the last resort: it only runs when there is no
better match and no global address on the interface. Drop the Kconfig
condition and use whatever link-local address the interface has.

Signed-off-by: Mala <mala.wolff00@gmail.com>
---
 subsys/net/ip/net_if.c | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/subsys/net/ip/net_if.c b/subsys/net/ip/net_if.c
index e92fb7f620..b1e9e41267 100644
--- a/subsys/net/ip/net_if.c
+++ b/subsys/net/ip/net_if.c
@@ -4268,9 +4268,12 @@ const struct net_in_addr *net_if_ipv4_select_src_addr(struct net_if *dst_iface,
 		src = net_if_ipv4_get_global_addr(dst_iface,
 						  NET_ADDR_PREFERRED);
 
-		if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_NET_IPV4_AUTO) && !src) {
+		if (!src) {
 			/* Try to use LL address if there's really no other
-			 * address available.
+			 * address available. This is not tied to
+			 * CONFIG_NET_IPV4_AUTO: an RFC 3927 address is equally
+			 * valid as a last-resort source when the application
+			 * configured it itself.
 			 */
 			src = net_if_ipv4_get_ll(dst_iface, NET_ADDR_PREFERRED);
 		}
-- 
